# Assignment 2 – Banking System

## Student
Name: Rinatuly Miras
Group: IT-2502

---

## Description
This project is a simple banking system written in Java.
It uses different data structures to simulate real banking operations.

---

## Data Structures Used

- **LinkedList** – stores all bank accounts
- **Stack** – stores transaction history (last in, first out)
- **Queue** – used for bill payments and account requests
- **Array** – used for fixed-size data (Task 6)

---

## Features

- Add account
- Deposit money
- Withdraw money
- Show all accounts
- View last transaction
- Undo last transaction
- Add and process bills
- Account request system

---

## Conclusion

This project shows how data structures like LinkedList, Stack, Queue, and Array are used in real applications such as banking systems.